{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Rank","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeIndependence"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jacobianRank_eq_three_of_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jacobianRank_eq_three_of_base","kind":"theorem","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L356-L363","doc":"**Rank-monotonicity principle.**  A rank function that is monotone\n(rank cannot drop when columns are added), bounded by the row count\n`3`, and equal to `3` at the base order is `3` at every order `≥ 3`.\nThis is the structural reason `full_rank` propagates from the base\norder without per-order computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jetJacobianBase_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jetJacobianBase_rank","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L351-L354","doc":"**Base-order full rank (PROVED, witnessed).**  The base minor is\ninvertible, hence has rank `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jetJacobianBase_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jetJacobianBase_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L346-L349","doc":"The base minor is invertible (`det = 1/16 ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jetJacobianBase_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jetJacobianBase_det","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L340-L344","doc":"The witnessed elimination determinant `det = 1/16 ≠ 0` (matches\n`jetOrder3_certificate`'s `∏ pivots = 1/16`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jetJacobianBase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jetJacobianBase","kind":"def","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L334-L338","doc":"Witnessed base-order jet-Jacobian: rows are the order-`≤2` coefficient\nvectors of `tr_M(K)` about `q = 1` for `K ∈ {4₁, 5₂, 𝓑₃}`.  Source:\n`computations/jet_order_pivots.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jetOrder3_certificate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jetOrder3_certificate","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L307-L313","doc":"**GB-elimination certificate at the Reid-1991 base order (PROVED,\nwitnessed).**  `∏ pivots = (1/4)·2·(1/8) = 1/16 ≠ 0` — the actual\nelimination determinant of the canonical Markov-trace jet-Jacobian — so\nthe order-3 Jacobian has full rank `3` and the three series are\njet-order independent at the base order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jetPivots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jetPivots","kind":"def","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L292-L305","doc":"GB-eliminated jet-order pivots, **witnessed from the framework's own\ncanonical Markov traces** (not representative).  The h-jet expansion\nabout `q = 1` of `tr_M(K)` for `K ∈ {4₁, 5₂, 𝓑₃}` (canonical braid\nwords `(σ₁σ₂⁻¹)²`, `σ₁⁻¹σ₂σ₁⁻¹σ₂²`, `(σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³`) gives the order-2\ncoefficient vectors `(1/4, −1, 55/16)`, `(1/2, 0, −1/16)`, `(1, 0, 0)`;\ntheir `3×3` jet-Jacobian has elimination determinant `1/16 ≠ 0`, with\nLU pivots `(1/4, 2, 1/8)`.  Source:\n`computations/jet_order_pivots.py` →\n`jet-order-pivots.witness.json`.  The constant extension certifies\nfull rank `3` at every order via `ofPivots`; higher-order pivots come\nfrom the same compute at higher jet truncation.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:three-knot-jet-order-independence ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence.ofPivots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence.ofPivots","kind":"def","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L277-L290","doc":"**`JetOrderIndependence` from a per-order GB certificate.**  Given that\nthe eliminated pivots are non-zero at every order `≥ 3`, the\n`full_rank` field is *proved* (not asserted) via the general\ncertificate `eliminationDet_ne_zero`.  Plug in the compute witness's\npivots to discharge the conjecture at every certified order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jacobianRankFromPivots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jacobianRankFromPivots","kind":"def","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L270-L275","doc":"`jacobianRank` defined *from* the certificate: full rank `3` exactly\nwhen the order-`N` pivot product is non-zero, else deficient.  This\nmakes `JetOrderIndependence.full_rank` a derived consequence of the\nGB certificate rather than a bare assertion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eliminationDet_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eliminationDet_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L259-L268","doc":"**GB-elimination certificate — general order (PROVED, sorry-free).**\nAt any order, three non-zero eliminated pivots give a non-singular\nechelon minor (non-zero determinant), hence full rank `3` and\njet-order independence at that order.  This is the order-uniform form\nof the certificate: every order is the same finite determinant test,\nparametric in the pivots the GB elimination produces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eliminationDet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eliminationDet","kind":"def","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L255-L257","doc":"The elimination determinant at one order = product of the three\nGB-eliminated pivots of the order-`N` minor of `(4₁, 5₂, 𝓑₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hyperbolicVolumeIndependence_of_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hyperbolicVolumeIndependence_of_reduction","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L216-L231","doc":"**Gap-closing reduction (§3b-cond conditional form).**\n\nThe deep algebraic-independence conjecture `HyperbolicVolumeIndependence`\nfollows from the two QOU-native inputs — finite jet-order independence\n(`full_rank`) and the surreal parallel-transport bound (reduced to its\ntwo named physical inputs (I2)+(I3), with (I1) + composition proved as\n`transport_shadow_vanishes`) — *modulo the bridge step*\n`JetTransportImpliesIndependence`.  It is a `def` (not an `instance`)\nto avoid competing with the standalone conjectural witness in\n`HyperbolicVolumeIndependence`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.JetTransportImpliesIndependence.nonempty_independence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetTransportImpliesIndependence.nonempty_independence","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L214-L214","doc":"The independence witness produced by the bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.JetTransportImpliesIndependence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetTransportImpliesIndependence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L211-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.JetTransportImpliesIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetTransportImpliesIndependence","kind":"class","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L194-L214","doc":"**Gap-closing reduction — the bridge step (§3b conjectural class).**\n\nThe Nesterenko-type transfer: *given* finite jet-order independence\nand the surreal parallel-transport bound, the full algebraic\nindependence `no_relation` follows.  The transfer from the finite\njet data + vanishing fibre shadow to the infinite-order polynomial\nstatement is the bridge's mathematical content; it is recorded as a\nconjectural class so the conditional structure is visible at every\ncall site (per §3b-cond).\n\n**History (2026-06-10).**  An earlier version \"derived\"\n`HyperbolicVolumeIndependence` here as a 5-line `def` — but only\nagainst a vacuous placeholder shape of that class\n(`residual = 0`), which made the reduction appear Lean-verified\nwhile carrying no mathematical content.  With the real class\n(`no_relation`, declared in `HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence` §7)\nthe bridge step is honestly conjectural. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.not_bound_of_physical_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.not_bound_of_physical_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L184-L190","doc":"**…and non-vacuous at any error with a non-zero physical shadow\n(PROVED).**  This is the content the parameterisation buys: for a\n*specific* `E` coming from the actual connection, the bound is a real\nconstraint that can fail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.trivialError_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.trivialError_bound","kind":"instance","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L177-L182","doc":"**The bound is vacuous at the zero error (PROVED).**  So an instance\n`[SurrealParallelTransportBound E]` for an *unspecified* `E` asserts\nnothing: it is satisfiable.  Any downstream result must say which `E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.trivialError","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.trivialError","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L170-L175","doc":"The identically-zero transport error. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.transport_uniform_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.transport_uniform_bound","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L152-L158","doc":"**(I1) Uniformity in jet order — PROVED (derived).**  With the per-order\nshadow vanishing, the transport error is uniformly bounded across all jet\norders (with constant `0`); no `N`-dependent blow-up can corrupt the limit\ntransfer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.transport_shadow_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.transport_shadow_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L143-L150","doc":"**(I3 ∘ I2 composition — PROVED).**  The total transport shadow of `E`\nvanishes at every order, from `E`'s structural decomposition together with\nboth parts' archimedean shadows vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.monodromy_archimedean_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.monodromy_archimedean_zero","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L137-L137","doc":"**(I3, second half) Monodromy is fibre-level.**  The cusp/modular\nmonodromy carries `Im(q)` structure but no real shadow.\n*Conjectural input.* ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.physical_archimedean_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.physical_archimedean_zero","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L133-L133","doc":"**(I2) Archimedean projection (fibre-vs-observable wall).**  The\nphysical part is a fibre-level surreal infinitesimal, so its\narchimedean shadow `τ`-projects to `0`.  *Conjectural input.* ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound.mk","kind":"ctor","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SurrealParallelTransportBound","kind":"class","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L123-L137","doc":"**Surreal parallel-transport bound (the bridge), as a predicate ON given\nerror data.**\n\nThe two conjectural inputs (I2) and (I3-second) are asserted *about the\nsupplied* `E`; the class can no longer manufacture its own shadow.\n(I1 uniformity and the composition are derived below.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.decomposes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.decomposes","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L121-L121","doc":"**(I3) Monodromy separation.**  The shadow splits into its physical and\nmonodromy parts.  This is a *structural* property of the supplied data,\nnot a conjectural input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.monodromy","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L117-L117","doc":"Cusp/modular-monodromy part of the shadow (the limit-only artifact). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.physical","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Physical-holonomy part of the shadow (the `→ Vol` contribution). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.shadow","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L113-L113","doc":"Archimedean (`τ`) shadow of the surreal transport error at order `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransportErrorData","kind":"structure","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L96-L121","doc":"**Transport-error data — the shadows as *given* data (2026-08-09).**\n\n`shadow N` is the archimedean (`τ`) realification of the fibre-level\nsurreal parallel-transport error on the projective state fibre `ℂP¹` at\njet order `N`, as `q` deforms toward the volume-conjecture limit, split\ninto its physical-holonomy (`→ Vol`) and cusp/modular-monodromy parts.\n\n**Why a structure and not class fields.**  The conjecture is about *one\nspecific* object — the transport error of the categorical connection.\nWhen the shadows are *fields of the class*, an instance gets to **choose**\nthe very functions it is supposed to constrain, and the constant-zero\nchoice satisfies everything by `rfl`.  That is precisely how the previous\nencoding was discharged for free.  Carrying them as data, and taking that\ndata as a **class parameter** below, forces every consumer to name the\nerror it is assuming about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence.full_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence.full_rank","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L94-L94","doc":"Full rank `3` from the base order onward (Reid-1991 anchors `N=3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence.jacobianRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence.jacobianRank","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L92-L92","doc":"Rank of the order-`N` coefficient Jacobian of the three series. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.JetOrderIndependence","kind":"class","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean#L82-L94","doc":"**Jet-order independence (weak, QOU-attackable conjecture).**\n\n`jacobianRank N` is the rank of the order-`N` cyclotomic-coefficient\nJacobian of the three coloured-Jones series `J_{4₁}, J_{5₂}, J_{𝓑₃}`\n(a `3 × (N+1)` matrix over `ℚ[q,q⁻¹]`). `full_rank` asserts it is the\nfull rank `3` from the Reid-1991 base order `N ≥ 3` onward — finite\nand decidable per order via a Gröbner–Shirshov elimination normal\nform. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:three-knot-jet-order-independence","label":"conj:three-knot-jet-order-independence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/three-knot-jet-order-independence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}